5. Is agricultural by-product collected and stored in a manner that
•   Collects or contains all leachate generated;
•   Diverts runoff from the storage structure and area;
•   Prevents contaminated runoff, leachate and solids from escaping;
•   If an escape occurs, contaminated runoff, leachate and solids do not enter surface water, groundwater or cross a property boundary;
•   Particulates do not cross a property boundary, and
•   Deters the attraction of, and access by, domestic pets, wildlife and vectors

8. If storing agricultural by-product in a new or modified storage structure in a vulnerable aquifer recharge area, are the following requirements met?
•   There is an impermeable base;
•   The impermeable base is maintained to prevent leakage;
•   Leakage assessments are carried out at least once every 6 months;
•   Corrective action is taken if any leaks are found, and
•   Records of maintenance and corrective actions are kept

